{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1010959-how-to-trick-exploit-a-true-fae-gentry","id":1010959,"title":"How to trick/exploit a True Fae/Gentry?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-01T23:48:05-08:00","id":1010959,"title":"How to trick/exploit a True Fae/Gentry?","content":"I recently watched a old Russian Fairy tale film called &quot;Jack Frost&quot; via MST3K and there's one scene where Baba Yaga is about to roast one of the protagonists and the he says &quot;wait wait I don't know how to properly sit on a griddle&quot; and then Baba Yaga stops and tells him how to sit on it and then he uses this to his advantage and throws her into the oven closes it up while throwing her tree hench men out of the door before letting her out.<br /> <br /> Which this got me thinking....perhaps is there a way to use a True Fae's alien mindset to your advantage and somehow exploit it like it's main weakness? Which almost like a Fairy Tale manner like using your wits to outsmart the True Fae sort of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-02-2016, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:41:36-08:00","id":1010996,"title":"","content":"I believe that's how most changelings escaped from the Fair Folk in the first place - especially the Grimms, who have an affinity with fairy tales in general.<br /> <br /> Approaches are also somewhat similar to this. The changeling imposes certain rules that the Gentry 